      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Mesh instancing is really good for achieving cool varied effects with minimal draw calls. I would love to see MaterialPropertyBlocks, DrawMeshInstanced(), and DrawMeshInstancedDirect() introduced into Udon.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-10-05T10:11:26.972Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It is always said that to get higher FPS, reducing draw calls is very important. And then, GPU Instancing is very useful to do it.\n\nIf we do nothing other than using GPU instancing, each instance would have almost same looks.\nBut , if we use Instanced Props and \nuse UnityEngine.MaterialPropertyBlock to override material's property which is defined as Instanced prop,we can draw many various objects at same time.\nPlease refer to Adding per-instance data :\nhttps://docs.unity3d.com/2018.1/Documentation/Manual/GPUInstancing.html",
